rows.en:
And then I was back in the reflection room.
"Are you all right, {a}?"
Iwashita glanced at my face.{p}

"Is something wrong with her hand?
She isn't holding anything, is she?"
Arai muttered under his breath.{p}

When I stepped into the hallway, Hashimoto was nowhere to be seen.
Where did she go?
Maybe I should try going back to the classroom.{p}

"Ah, wait a second!"
As I reached out to catch her, the textbook fell from my hand.
When she saw it, her face went rigid.{p}

"That's..."
She pointed at the textbook on the floor.
Can she tell it's Kawahara's textbook?{p}

"It's not that I want to curse anyone.
I did something terrible to Kawahara.
I'm not allowed to go on living."{p}

...Behind her as she said it, a teacher I'd never seen before appeared.
"Hashimoto, what are you doing?
You were supposed to report to the reflection room today."{p}

"Hashimoto!"
I tried to tear up the apology lying in front of her.
The moment I did, I was engulfed in a blinding light.{p}

No, I can't get near her☆
What's happening?
My head hurts☆{p}

..................When the light died down and I opened my eyes, Fukuzawa was peering down at me.
"Thank goodness, {b}.
I thought you were never going to wake up."{p}
